  "explanation": "A full batch needs batchSize items starting at each index, so valid start indexes run from 0 up to items.length - batchSize inclusive. The loop's strict `< items.length - batchSize` skips that last valid start, so it counts 2 full batches instead of 3.",
  "prompt": "This counts how many full batches of a given size can be shipped from a load list. Step through the loop and predict what it prints.",
